{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CROSS-REFERENCE: the plumbing defect is now tracked as **b690-f232-5bae-4b8b** (antifungal-pine-swan), a BUG parented under epic 061c and linked as BLOCKING this ticket. Operator confirmed the plumbing fix is in scope for the epic.\n\nWHY IT BLOCKS: this ticket's last criterion asks for a live run showing per-pass model ids matching the declarations. That run currently DISPROVES the behaviour, and no amount of evidence-gathering here can change that until b690 lands. This ticket's YAML work is complete and correct (Gerrit 1169, +1/+1) — it is the runtime that ignores it.\n\nA THIRD hypothesis was eliminated after the previous comment, so the diagnosis is now airtight: H3 \"the class table falls back to built-in defaults under the snapshot read root\" predicts `verify` (declaring `standard`) runs on `claude-sonnet-4-6`, because `_DEFAULT_MODEL_BY_CLASS['standard']` IS sonnet. It ran on OPUS. Only \"the step's model: is never consulted\" predicts opus for a step declaring standard. H2 (config not loaded) was eliminated separately. Recorded on b690 in full."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785608567632490001,"uuid":"4bd872c3-2754-4aa8-8abc-5be5250ce3b5"}